{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "cd0fef14-c7a7-4b41-8ca9-0063b328f743",
    "name": "Amendment Service",
    "description": "Customer-initiated account amendments — the generated Kogito process API.\n\nThe scenarios under 'Routing' are the point: identical requests differing in one field take different paths through the same process definition. Run them in order and watch the Console tab.\n\nSet {{baseUrl}} in the collection variables (default http://localhost:8090).\n\nInstance and task ids are captured automatically by the test scripts, so the follow-up requests work without copying ids by hand.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "36662669"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Service health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/actuator/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "actuator",
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "UP means the service is running and connected to Postgres."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Routing scenarios",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Verified address — straight through",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('requestInstanceId', b.id);",
                  "pm.test('created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('one item permitted', () => pm.expect(b.amendmentItems).to.have.lengthOf(1));",
                  "console.log('Route: intake -> screening -> admissibility -> CoA child -> core banking -> complete');",
                  "console.log('Item admissibility:', b.amendmentItems[0].admissibility);",
                  "console.log('Address verified:', b.amendmentItems[0].coa.addressVerified);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"requestId\": \"REQ-VERIFIED\",\n  \"amendmentType\": \"COA\",\n  \"accountStatus\": \"ACTIVE\",\n  \"requestorIsParty\": true,\n  \"mandatePermits\": true,\n  \"channel\": \"DIGITAL\",\n  \"screeningOutcome\": \"CLEAR\",\n  \"inFlightAmendment\": false,\n  \"accountIsJoint\": false,\n  \"riskBand\": \"LOW\",\n  \"addressVerified\": true\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/amendment_request",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "amendment_request"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The address is already verified, so the CoA child skips the evidence branch and applies the change in core banking. The instance completes."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Unverified address — parks at a human task",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('requestInstanceId', b.id);",
                  "pm.test('created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "console.log('Route: same as scenario 1 until the CoA child, then the evidence branch');",
                  "console.log('Address verified:', b.amendmentItems[0].coa.addressVerified);",
                  "console.log('Next: run \"List CoA instances\" then \"List tasks\" to see it waiting.');"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"requestId\": \"REQ-UNVERIFIED\",\n  \"amendmentType\": \"COA\",\n  \"accountStatus\": \"ACTIVE\",\n  \"requestorIsParty\": true,\n  \"mandatePermits\": true,\n  \"channel\": \"DIGITAL\",\n  \"screeningOutcome\": \"CLEAR\",\n  \"inFlightAmendment\": false,\n  \"accountIsJoint\": false,\n  \"riskBand\": \"LOW\",\n  \"addressVerified\": false\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/amendment_request",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "amendment_request"
              ]
            },
            "description": "One field differs from scenario 1. The address is unverified, so the CoA child requests proof of address and the instance waits at a user task instead of completing."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Change of name — screening and approval",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('requestInstanceId', b.id);",
                  "console.log('Route: dispatched to the CoN child rather than CoA');",
                  "console.log('Item type:', b.amendmentItems[0].type);"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"requestId\": \"REQ-NAME\",\n  \"amendmentType\": \"CON\",\n  \"accountStatus\": \"ACTIVE\",\n  \"requestorIsParty\": true,\n  \"mandatePermits\": true,\n  \"channel\": \"BRANCH\",\n  \"screeningOutcome\": \"CLEAR\",\n  \"inFlightAmendment\": false,\n  \"accountIsJoint\": false,\n  \"riskBand\": \"LOW\",\n  \"nameChangeReason\": \"MARRIAGE\",\n  \"rescreenOutcome\": \"CLEAR\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/amendment_request",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "amendment_request"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The routing gateway sends this to the change of name child process. It collects evidence, re-screens under the new name, and requires maker-checker approval."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Name change with a screening hit",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"requestId\": \"REQ-NAME-HIT\",\n  \"amendmentType\": \"CON\",\n  \"accountStatus\": \"ACTIVE\",\n  \"requestorIsParty\": true,\n  \"mandatePermits\": true,\n  \"channel\": \"BRANCH\",\n  \"screeningOutcome\": \"CLEAR\",\n  \"inFlightAmendment\": false,\n  \"accountIsJoint\": false,\n  \"riskBand\": \"LOW\",\n  \"nameChangeReason\": \"DEED_POLL\",\n  \"rescreenOutcome\": \"CONFIRMED_HIT\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/amendment_request",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "amendment_request"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Re-screening under the new name returns a hit, so the child routes to financial crime disposition before approval rather than straight to it."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "5. Joint to sole — consent granted",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"requestId\": \"REQ-JTS\",\n  \"amendmentType\": \"JOINT_TO_SOLE\",\n  \"accountStatus\": \"ACTIVE\",\n  \"requestorIsParty\": true,\n  \"mandatePermits\": true,\n  \"channel\": \"BRANCH\",\n  \"screeningOutcome\": \"CLEAR\",\n  \"inFlightAmendment\": false,\n  \"accountIsJoint\": true,\n  \"riskBand\": \"LOW\",\n  \"allConsentsGranted\": true,\n  \"remainingPartyEligible\": true,\n  \"jointLiabilities\": true\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/amendment_request",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "amendment_request"
              ]
            },
            "description": "A joint account converting to sole. Every departing party has consented, so the conversion proceeds to approval."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "6. Joint to sole — party deceased, diverted",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"requestId\": \"REQ-JTS-BEREAVEMENT\",\n  \"amendmentType\": \"JOINT_TO_SOLE\",\n  \"accountStatus\": \"ACTIVE\",\n  \"requestorIsParty\": true,\n  \"mandatePermits\": true,\n  \"channel\": \"BRANCH\",\n  \"screeningOutcome\": \"CLEAR\",\n  \"inFlightAmendment\": false,\n  \"accountIsJoint\": true,\n  \"riskBand\": \"LOW\",\n  \"otherPartyStatus\": \"DECEASED\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/amendment_request",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "amendment_request"
              ]
            },
            "description": "A party is deceased. The eligibility decision diverts this to the bereavement journey rather than processing it as a conversion — the behaviour ADR-001 specifies."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "7. Multiple amendments in one request",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"requestId\": \"REQ-MULTI\",\n  \"accountStatus\": \"ACTIVE\",\n  \"requestorIsParty\": true,\n  \"mandatePermits\": true,\n  \"channel\": \"BRANCH\",\n  \"screeningOutcome\": \"CLEAR\",\n  \"inFlightAmendment\": false,\n  \"accountIsJoint\": false,\n  \"riskBand\": \"LOW\",\n  \"includesCoa\": true,\n  \"includesCon\": true,\n  \"addressVerified\": true,\n  \"rescreenOutcome\": \"CLEAR\",\n  \"amendmentType\": \"COA\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/amendment_request",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "amendment_request"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Address and name change in one request. The dispatch loop fans out to both child processes — one case, two amendments."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "Each scenario differs from the others by one or two fields and takes a different path."
    },
